    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered list for `POST /api/owners`, as the code actually stands. The active path is entirely the OfficeFloor pipeline defined in `src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml` \u2014 there is no Spring `@RestController` left.\n\n## Gate (before the pipeline runs)\n\n1. **Authorization** \u2014 `composition.authorize: \"hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')\"`. No role \u2192 403 (`ForbiddenExceptionHandler`).\n2. **Bean validation of the request DTO** (`OwnerFieldsDto`), surfaced as `MethodArgumentNotValidException` \u2192 400:\n   - `firstName` `@NotNull`, `@Pattern` (letters, up to 3 words), `@Size 1\u201330`\n   - `lastName` `@NotNull`, `@Pattern`, `@Size 1\u201330`\n   - `city` `@NotNull`, `@Size 1\u201380`\n   - `telephone` `@NotNull`, `@Pattern ^[0-9]*$`, `@Size 1\u201320`\n   - `address`/`addressLine1` `@Size 1\u2013255`, `addressLine2` `@Size \u2264255`, `email` `@Size \u2264255`, `postcode` `@Pattern ^[0-9]{4}$`\n\n## Pipeline steps, in execution order\n\n3. **`CheckIdempotencyKey`** \u2014 reads `Idempotency-Key` header. If seen before \u2192 branch to **`ReplayCreatedOwner`** (loads existing owner, responds **200**, short-circuiting everything below). Otherwise continues to validate.\n4. **`RequireOwnerFields`** \u2014 *side-effect first:* `OwnerAddress.normalizeInPlace(request)` mutates the address on the request; then requires non-blank firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException` (400, lists missing fields).\n5. **`RejectFutureRegistrationDate`** \u2014 if `registrationDate` present and after now \u2192 400.\n6. **`ValidatePostcode`** \u2014 if present, must be `^[0-9]{4}$` and fall in the city's region range (Sydney 2000\u20132099 / Melbourne 3000\u20133099 / Brisbane 4000\u20134099) \u2192 400.\n7. **`NormalizeOwnerTelephone`** \u2014 *side-effect:* rewrites telephone to E.164 in place.\n8. **`ValidateTelephoneCountryLength`** \u2014 national-number length check (+61 \u2192 9 digits, +1 \u2192 10) \u2192 400.\n9. **`NormalizeOwnerEmail`** \u2014 *side-effect:* blank\u2192null, lower-cased; if non-blank must match the email regex \u2192 400.\n10. **`RejectDisposableEmailDomain`** \u2014 blocks mailinator.com / tempmail.com / guerrillamail.com \u2192 400.\n11. **`RejectCityAtCapacity`** \u2014 \u226550 owners in same city \u2192 409.\n12. **`RejectDailyLimit`** \u2014 \u2265100 owners on the effective (business-day-rolled) registration date \u2192 429.\n\n## Transactional segment (`govern: [transaction]`, commits once at the end)\n\n13. **`BuildOwner`** \u2014 *side-effect:* maps DTO\u2192`Owner`; sets `registrationDate` rolled to a business day.\n14. **`AssignNamesakeCount`** \u2014 *side-effect:* sets `namesakeCount` (non-deleted owners sharing first+last name).\n15. **`AssignCustomerCode`** \u2014 *side-effect:* sets `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, de-duplicated with `-2`, `-3`, \u2026\n16. **`AssignHousehold`** \u2014 *side-effect:* sets `householdId` = first 12 hex of SHA-256(lastName|postcode).\n17. **`RejectDuplicateIdentity`** \u2014 unless `sharesHousehold=true`, another non-deleted owner with the same `householdId` \u2192 409.\n18. **`AssignPossibleDuplicate`** \u2014 *side-effect:* sets `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf` when same lastName+postcode but different phone (skipped if `sharesHousehold`).\n19. **`AssignHouseholdSize`** \u2014 *side-effect:* sets `householdSize` (household members + 1).\n20. **`SaveOwner`** \u2014 *side-effect:* persists the owner (id assigned).\n21. **`AuditOwnerCreated`** \u2014 *side-effect:* logs to the AUDIT logger (id, customerCode, registrationDate, membership fields).\n22. **`RecordIdempotencyKey`** \u2014 *side-effect:* if a key was supplied, records `key \u2192 owner.id` in the idempotency store.\n23. **`RespondWithOwnerCreated`** \u2014 maps to `OwnerDto` (also sets `bulkSignupWarning`) and responds **201 Created** with a `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header.\n\n## Notes worth flagging\n\n- **The DTO `telephone` bean-validation regex (`^[0-9]*$`, step 2) conflicts with the E.164 form** the pipeline normalizes to. Bean validation runs on the raw input (digits-only), so a `+`-prefixed submission would be rejected at the gate before normalization ever runs \u2014 input must be plain digits, and the entity's own `@Pattern` (`^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$`) expects the normalized `+` form.\n- `RejectCityAtCapacity` counts via `findAll()` **without filtering soft-deleted** owners, unlike the other counts (namesake/household/duplicate) which exclude deleted.\n- Entity JPA lifecycle callbacks (`@PrePersist` etc.) and `Owner.addPet` are **not** on this path \u2014 all side-effects are in the pipeline functions.\n\nWant me to dig into any specific step's exact logic?"
